{"path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment1.md","content":"🚨 **BLOCKING: XSS — snapshot `tokens[].leg` interpolated into a `title` attribute without `esc()`**

`flowHtml` builds the board-level token chip with the leg names interpolated **raw** into the `title` attribute:

```js
chips.push('<span class="flow-chip" title="' +
  Object.keys(s.tokens.legs).map(function (k) {
    return k + ' ' + fmtK(s.tokens.legs[k].total);
  }).join(', ') +
  '">...
```

A leg name containing `"` breaks out of the attribute and injects attributes/markup:

```html
<span class="flow-chip" title="x" onmouseover="alert(1) 42k"><b>Σ tok</b></span>
```

Every sibling interpolation in this PR escapes the same data — `tokChipHtml` wraps the legs string in `esc(legs)`, `drawerFlowHtml` uses `esc(k)` — and the file's own threat model (the `?fixture=` guard comment: "attacker-controlled cards under our origin") declares snapshot card data untrusted. `js/factoryState.js` `normTokenRow` stringifies `leg` from arbitrary report input (`r.leg == null ? null : String(r.leg)`), so this sink accepts whatever the snapshot carries.

Fix — one call, matching the convention used everywhere else:

```js
chips.push('<span class="flow-chip" title="' +
  esc(Object.keys(s.tokens.legs).map(function (k) {
    return k + ' ' + fmtK(s.tokens.legs[k].total);
  }).join(', ')) +
  '">...
```
"}

{"path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment2.md","content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: legs buckets keyed by raw `leg` — `__proto__`/`constructor` keys silently corrupt the totals**

`tokenTotals` buckets per leg with a plain `{}` and a truthiness check:

```js
var leg = r.leg || '—';
var b = out.legs[leg];
if (!b) { b = out.legs[leg] = { prompt: 0, completion: 0, total: 0 }; }
b.prompt += p; ...
```

`normTokenRow` only stringifies `leg`, it doesn't constrain it, so:

- `leg: "__proto__"` — the assignment sets the prototype of `out.legs`; the leg vanishes from `Object.keys` (per-leg chips/drawer table) while `out.total` still counts its rows.
- `leg: "constructor"` — `out.legs['constructor']` is the inherited `Object` function (truthy), so `b.prompt += p` writes `NaN` properties onto the `Object` constructor and the leg disappears from the per-leg view.

`flowSummary`'s cross-card merge (line ~246) repeats the same pattern. Machine leg names are agent contextIds today, so this is hardening, not an live bug — but it's a brand-new pure module and the fix is one line:

```js
var legs = Object.create(null);           // or: if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(out.legs, leg))
```
"}

{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: `entriesOf` dropped the chronological sort the old `cardHistory` had**

The removed v3 `cardHistory` sorted entries by timestamp (`entries.sort(...)` with nulls first); `entriesOf` preserves snapshot order and `phaseRail` computes durations positionally (`next.at - e.at`, clamped by `Math.max(0, …)`). The machine's `nextHistory` appends chronologically, so normal snapshots are fine — but hand-edited fixtures (like `visual-check/fixture.json`, edited in this very PR) or any legacy/older snapshot with out-of-order entries now render clamped-to-0 durations and misattribute rework rounds silently instead of being corrected. Cheap to keep the old guarantee:

```js
return mapped.sort(function (a, b) {
  return (a.at == null ? 0 : a.at) - (b.at == null ? 0 : b.at);
});
```

(Or document why order is trusted now.)
